<problem>
<!-- <title>discrete equilibria 5</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" from="1" to=" 10" />

<selectFromSequence name="c" from="1" to=" 33" />
<select name="x"> x y z u v w p X Y Z S</select>

<math name="answer" unordered="true">$a[1] ,$a[2] </math>
<math name="twob" simplify="full">2*$a[2] </math>
<math name="bsquare" simplify="full">$a[2] **2</math>

</setup>


<p>Find all equilibria to the discrete dynamical system below.  If there are multiple equilibria, separate your answers by commas.  
<md>
  <mrow>$x _{n+1}  - $x _n \amp = ($x _n - $a[1]  )( $x _n^2 - $twob $x _n + $bsquare  )</mrow>
  <mrow>$x _0 \amp = $c</mrow>
</md>
</p>

<p><m>E =</m> 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$answer </award>
</answer>
</p>


<solution>
<p>To find the equilibria, we set <m>$x _{n+1} = E</m> and <m>$x _n = E</m> in the evolution rule, obtaining
<md>
  <mrow>E-E\amp =  ( E - $a[1]  )( E^2 - $twob E + $bsquare  )</mrow>
  <mrow>0\amp = ( E - $a[1]  )( E^2 - $twob E + $bsquare  )</mrow>
</md>
We can factor the quadratic: <m>( E^2 - $twob E + $bsquare  )  = (E-$a[2] )^2</m>.  The condition for the equilibria becomes
<me>0 = ( E - $a[1]  ) (E-$a[2] )^2.</me>
Therefore, the equilibria are <m>E=$a[1] </m> and <m>E = $a[2] </m>.</p>


</solution>


</problem>